<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Results</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Harness.Results</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    DB-8, the result package. Filed under build-plan 6.4 and brought forward because PHASE 5's exit
    criterion depends on it: "a block goes from request to tested without a human in the inner loop,
    AND the result package tells the authoring agent something it could act on." A bare pass/fail
    cannot satisfy the second half.

    THE ONE PROPERTY EVERYTHING HERE SERVES: *** A RESULT MUST BE UNABLE TO LOOK CONCLUSIVE WHEN IT
    IS NOT. *** Every not-conclusive state is modelled as its own thing rather than as an absent
    field, because an absent field reads as "fine" to everyone who did not write it.

    It sits ABOVE the wire: it consumes what a run produced and what a submission declared, and it
    opens no socket and derives no address.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Wire\Harness.Wire.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
